# Trivy exceptions for packages removed from the final runtime filesystem.
# The Python runtime image inherits global pip/setuptools dependencies from the
# upstream python:3.12-slim layer. The application runs only from /opt/venv,
# where the affected packages are upgraded to fixed versions. The vulnerable
# global packages are removed from the final filesystem; Trivy can still report
# their metadata because it scans image layers. Keep these IDs exact and review
# them whenever the runtime base image changes.
